# Overview — README.md (L1)

Project: Kryon — autonomous cybersecurity agent, AGPL-3.0, v2.1.0. 110 playbooks + 362 function tools (per badges). Local-first; skill-based; three execution modes.

## Section map (line numbers)
- 31 What is KRYON — pitch + capabilities (compliance audit, pentest, DFIR/incident response).
- 68 Quickstart — install + first run.
- 109 Execution modes — the three modes.
- 194 Skill System — playbook/skill architecture (110 playbooks), how skills load.
- 278 Workflow — end-to-end flow.
- 303 Architecture — components (362 function tools), the stack.
- 388 Installation — detailed, long (multiple platforms/stacks).
- 625 Supported AI Models — model backends.
- 639 Compliance Coverage — standards mapped (CIS etc.).
- 672 Docker Stack — containers (kryon Kali box et al.).
- 697 Testing · 715 Contributing · 727 Disclaimer · 735 License (AGPL-3.0).

## Quick facts
- Entry point to the repo: read "What is KRYON" + "Skill System" first.
- The Docker Stack section documents the kryon Kali container that hosts the offensive toolset.
- Compliance section references CIS controls (related importer scripts live in scripts/).
